4. BACKEND API CONTRACT (do not invent endpoints)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Base URL: VITE_API_BASE_URL (default http://localhost:8000)
CORS is open. All responses are JSON except zone GeoJSON (also JSON).
Errors: 404 unknown zone/region, 422 invalid horizon, 503 data not ready.

GET /health
  -> { status: "ok" | "no_data", synthetic_data: boolean, data_dir: string,
       data_date?: "YYYY-MM-DD" }

GET /regions
  -> { regions: ["pune"] }

GET /summary?region=pune
  -> { city, data_date, weights: {hazard, exposure, vulnerability},
       class_counts_now: { Low?, Moderate?, High?, Critical? },
       mean_score_now: number, mean_score_h3: number,
       population_in_high_or_critical: number }

GET /zones?region=pune&horizon=0|24|48|72&min_class=Low|Moderate|High|Critical
           &w_hazard=&w_exposure=&w_vulnerability=
  -> GeoJSON FeatureCollection with 136 features and a `meta` object:
     {
       type: "FeatureCollection",
       features: [{
         type: "Feature",
         geometry: { type: "Polygon", coordinates: number[][][] },
         properties: {
           cell_id: string, horizon_days: 0|1|2|3, date: "YYYY-MM-DD",
           score: number, risk_class: "Low"|"Moderate"|"High"|"Critical",
           hazard: number, exposure: number, vulnerability: number,
           pm25: number, aqi_est: number, population: number,
           top_factors: string[], forecast_drivers: Driver[]
         }
       }],
       meta: { horizon_days, weights, custom_weights: boolean, data_date, count }
     }
  NOTE: horizon is in hours (0/24/48/72). Weight params override the score server-side.

GET /priority-queue?region=pune&horizon=&limit=&risk_class=
                    &w_hazard=&w_exposure=&w_vulnerability=
  -> PriorityRow[]
     {
       cell_id, lat, lon, pop, industry_frac, emit_5km,
       top_factors: string[],
       score_now, score_h1, score_h2, score_h3, score_ranked,
       trend, risk_class, action, rank, priority_index
     }
  Omitting horizon ranks by the worst of now..+72h.

GET /zones/{cell_id}
  -> {
       cell_id, geometry, current: ZoneProperties,
       centroid: { lat, lon },
       priority: PriorityRow,
       scores: { h0, h1, h2, h3 },
       components: { hazard, exposure, vulnerability },
       points: { pts_pollution, pts_emission, pts_population,
                 pts_wind, pts_green, pts_heat },
       top_factors: string[],
       forecast_drivers: Driver[],
       history: { dates: string[], pm25: number[],
                  forecast_dates: string[], forecast_pm25: number[] }
     }

GET /forecast/{cell_id}
  -> {
       cell_id,
       history: { dates: string[], pm25: number[] },
       forecast: [{ horizon_days: 1|2|3, date, pm25, score, risk_class }],
       forecast_drivers: Driver[]
     }

GET /wind?region=pune
  -> [{ cell_id, lat, lon, wind_u, wind_v, wind_speed, wind_dir }]

GET /alerts?min_level=watch|warning|critical
  -> [{
       alert_id, zone_id, level: "watch"|"warning"|"critical",
       message, created_at, score_now, score_peak, population,
       drivers: string[], recommended_action, rank
     }]

POST /alerts/notify
  body: { channel: "telegram"|"email", min_level, dry_run: boolean }
  -> dry_run: { sent: false, count, text }
     live:    { sent: boolean, count, channel }

POST /weights
  body: { hazard: number, exposure: number, vulnerability: number,
          horizon: 0..3, top: 1..100 }
  -> {
       weights: { hazard, exposure, vulnerability },
       horizon_days, class_counts: Record<RiskClass, number>, mean_score,
       zones: ZonesFeatureCollection,
       priority_queue: PriorityRow[]
     }

GET /model/metrics
  -> {
       time_cut, n_features, xgboost: boolean,
       results: {
         h1: { persistence, random_forest, xgboost, spatial_holdout },
         h2: { ... }, h3: { ... }
       }
     }
  Each model object: { MAE, RMSE, R2, AQI_category_acc }.

GET /model/shap
  -> { method: "shap", global: [{ feature, label, mean_abs }] }

Shared type:
  Driver = { feature: string, label: string, value: number,
             shap: number, text: string }

Optional static asset (not an API): /data/emitters.json is an array of
  [lat, lon, weight]. Render subtle emitter dots only if the file exists.

